<div class="section" id="g_t_041e_0431_043d_043e_0432_0438_0442_044c-Postgres-_0434_043b_044f-Cuirass">
<div class="header">
<p>
Up: <a href="Upravlenie-sistemoi-Guix.html" accesskey="u" rel="up">Управление системой Guix</a> &nbsp; [<a href="index.html#SEC_Contents" title="Table of contents" rel="contents">Contents</a>][<a href="Terminy-i-ukazateli.html" title="Index" rel="index">Index</a>]</p>
</div>
<hr />
<span id="Obnovitx-Postgres-dlya-Cuirass"></span><h3 class="section">11.1 Обновить Postgres для Cuirass</h3>

<p>With the deprecation of the default value for the postgres package in
postgresql-configuration (see b93434e656eba4260df82158a96c295000d3ff44),
system upgrades need some manual action before they can take place.  Here&rsquo;s
a handy guide on how to.
</p>
<p>Please note that this is a straight-forward way for smaller datasets.  For
larger databases
<a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/pgupgrade.html"><code>pg_upgrade</code></a> may be the better choice.  Handling the service and
system upgrade as described in this guide still applies, though.
</p>
<ol>
<li> Stop and disable cuirass.

<p>Prevent the service from starting and failing after a reconfiguration:
</p>
<p><code>sudo herd stop cuirass &amp;&amp; sudo herd disable cuirass</code>
</p>
</li><li> Dump the database contents.

<p><code>sudo su - postgres -s /bin/sh -c pg_dumpall &gt; /tmp/pg.dump</code>
</p>
</li><li> Add or alter the postgres service.

<p>Depending on whether your postgres service is defined implicitly (through
the dependency from the cuirass service) or its own entry in your operating
system&rsquo;s <code>(services)</code> property, you need to either add or alter the
already existing configuration to reflect your intended version upgrade.
</p>
<p>Be careful not to upgrade directly to postgres-16 &ndash; cuirass service for
some reason doesn&rsquo;t like that.  I had to find and purge the relevant files
and then re-initialize after a failed upgrade to postgres 16.
</p>
<div class="example lisp">
<pre class="lisp"><span class="syntax-paren0">(<span class="syntax-symbol"><a class="syntax-symbol" href="/manual/devel/ru/html_node/Interfeis-servisa.html#index-service">service</a> <a class="syntax-symbol" href="/manual/devel/ru/html_node/Servisy-baz-dannykh.html#index-postgresql_002dservice_002dtype">postgresql-service-type</a>
         <span class="syntax-paren1">(<span class="syntax-symbol"><span class="syntax-symbol">postgresql-configuration</span>
          <span class="syntax-paren2">(<span class="syntax-symbol"><span class="syntax-symbol">postgresql</span> <span class="syntax-paren3">(<span class="syntax-symbol"><a class="syntax-symbol" href="https://www.gnu.org/software/guile/manual/html_node/Using-Guile-Modules.html#index-_0040">@</a> <span class="syntax-paren4">(<span class="syntax-symbol"><span class="syntax-symbol">gnu</span> <span class="syntax-symbol">packages</span> <span class="syntax-symbol">databases</span></span>)</span> <span class="syntax-symbol">postgresql-15</span></span>)</span></span>)</span></span>)</span></span>)</span>
</pre></div>

<p>Note: If you for some reason didn&rsquo;t read the text here but somewhat blindly
followed the examples and <em>did upgrade to 16</em>, here&rsquo;s how you reset the
state:
</p>
<ol>
<li> Delete the database instance files.

<p>They default to live under <samp>/var/lib/postgres/data</samp>.
</p>
</li><li> Re-initialize postgres.

<p><code>sudo su - postgres -s /bin/sh -c 'pg_ctl init -D /var/lib/postgres/data'</code>
</p></li></ol>

</li><li> Reconfigure your system.

<p><code>sudo guix system reconfigure path/to/your/altered/config.scm</code>
</p>
</li><li> Restore database contents.

<p><code>sudo su - postgres -s /bin/sh -c 'psql -d postgres -f /tmp/pg.dump'</code>
</p>
</li><li> Enable and start the service.

<div class="example">
<pre class="example">sudo herd enable cuirass
sudo herd start cuirass
</pre></div>

</li></ol>


</div>
<hr />
